  "description": "In this rendition of braised collard greens, we replace bacon with another deeply savory ingredient: smoked turkey.",
  "notes": "Notes: To make smoked turkey stock, add one pound of bones from a smoked turkey carcass to a large pot. Add a roughly chopped onion, carrot, and celery stalk, along with two bay leaves. Cover with water and simmer for two hours. Strain and discard solids. Homemade or store-bought low-sodium chicken stock can be used in place of the smoked turkey stock.",
